{title: 346 - Lord, Who Dost Give to Thy Church}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #346 • SEVENTH AND JAMES • 11.10.11.11}
{lyricist: Ernest A. Payne}
{composer: Charles F. Brown}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 346}
{meta: tune SEVENTH AND JAMES}
{meta: meter 11.10.11.11}
{meta: category Christian Church - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Cm/G]Lord, [Fm]who [Gm]dost [Bb]give [Ab]to [Gm]Thy [Ab]church [Gm]for [Fm]its [Gm]healing
[Eb]Gifts, [Gm/D]and [Eb]the [Gm]grace [Fm]to [Ddim]sustain and [Cm]renew,
[Bb]Hear [Eb]as we [Ab]pray [Gm/D]that today [Cm]and each [Fm]morrow
[Fm/C]We to [Ddim]Thy [Fm]purpose [Gm]may [Cm]show [Ab]ourselves [Eb]true.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Cm/G]Clear [Fm]be [Gm]the [Bb]voices [Gm]of [Ab]preachers [Fm]and [Gm]prophets
[Eb]Fearlessly [Gm]speaking [Ddim]the [Eb]word [Ddim]of [Cm]the [Fm]Lord,
[Bb]Word [Eb]of redemption [Gm/D]thro'God's [Cm]Son incarnate,
[Fm/C]Blessing for [Gm]cursing, [Cm]and [Ab]peace [Gm]for [Fm]the [Eb]sword.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Cm/G]Tender [Gm]and [Bb]wise [Ab]be [Gm]the [Ab]hearts [Gm]of [Fm]the [Gm]pastors,
[Eb]Guiding and [Gm]guarding [Ddim]the [Eb]souls [Ddim]in [Cm]their [Fm]care,
[Bb]Firm [Eb]with the [Ab]wayward, [Gm/D]a strength [Cm]to the [Fm]doubting,
[Fm/C]Helping the [Gm]needy [Cm]their [Ab]burdens [Fm]to [Eb]bear.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Cm/G]May [Fm]those [Gm]who [Bb]teach [Ab]grow [Gm]in [Ab]knowledge [Fm]and [Gm]patience,
[Eb]Guiding to [Gm]wisdom [Ddim]the [Eb]young [Ddim]and [Cm]the [Fm]old,
[Bb]Training [Eb]for [Ab]worship [Gm/D]and witness [Cm]and [Fm]service,
[Fm/C]Foes to [Ddim]all [Fm]falsehood, [Cm]in [Ab]truthfulness [Eb]bold.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Cm/G]Lord, [Fm]ever [Bb]give [Ab]to [Gm]us [Ab]gifts [Gm]in [Fm]due [Gm]measure,
[Eb]Each [Gm/D]needing other, [Ddim]and [Eb]all [Ddim]having [Fm]worth;
[Bb]So [Eb]to the [Ab]Father, [Gm/D]the Son, [Cm]and the [Fm]Spirit,
[Fm/C]Glory be [Gm]shown by [Cm]the [Ab]church [Gm]here [Fm]on [Eb]earth.
{end_of_verse}
